{
  "text": "```verilog\nmodule areset_deassert_sync #(\n    parameter CHAINS = 2,\n    parameter RST_POL = 1'b1\n)(\n    input  clk,\n    input  async_rst_i,\n    output sync_rst_o\n);\n\n    // Normalize the reset polarity so that internally we work with an\n    // active-high asynchronous reset signal.\n    wire async_rst_norm = RST_POL ? async_rst_i : ~async_rst_i;\n\n    // Synchronizer chain for the deassertion (release) of the reset.\n    // The chain is reset asynchronously by the normalized reset, so that\n    // when the reset is asserted, the chain is forced to 0 (inactive).\n    // When the reset deasserts, the chain will asynchronously clear to 0,\n    // and then on subsequent clock edges it will synchronously propagate\n    // the deasserted state (1) through the chain.\n    //\n    // After CHAINS clock cycles following the deassertion of async_rst_i,\n    // the last stage of the chain will be 1, indicating a safe release.\n    //\n    // sync_rst_o is active when the reset is asserted OR when the release\n    // has not yet completed (i.e., the last stage of the chain is 0).\n\n    reg [CHAINS-1:0] sync_chain;\n\n    integer i;\n    always @(posedge clk or posedge async_rst_norm) begin\n        if (async_rst_norm)\n            sync_chain <= {CHAINS{1'b0}};\n        else\n            for (i = 0; i < CHAINS; i = i + 1) begin\n                if (i == 0)\n                    sync_chain[i] <= 1'b1;\n                else\n                    sync_chain[i] <= sync_chain[i-1];\n            end\n    end\n\n    // The output is active (reset asserted) if:\n    // 1. The asynchronous reset is currently asserted, OR\n    // 2. The release pipeline has not yet completed (last stage is 0).\n    //\n    // When async_rst_norm is 1, sync_rst_o is 1 (active).\n    // When async_rst_norm is 0, sync_rst_o follows ~sync_chain[CHAINS-1],\n    // which is 1 until the chain has fully propagated the deassertion.\n\n    assign sync_rst_o = RST_POL ? (async_rst_norm | ~sync_chain[CHAINS-1])\n                                : (async_rst_norm | ~sync_chain[CHAINS-1]);\n\nendmodule\n```<|im_end|>",
